# Ruling D8 as a counterfactual. The base `counterfactual/receipt-certifies-safety`
# puts the material-security receipt route back on `secure`, the single item
# safety and material security were before the split. The same receipt that
# shows Yenna received essential goods then concludes that Yenna is safe: a
# service record standing in for bodily safety. On the live source the receipt
# concludes material security only, and bodily safety has no receipt route.
:expect-pins 4

? secure(Yenna).
# => TRUE
? suffice(Yenna).
# => FALSE

# The firewall is unchanged either way: confinement for lacking either item is
# refused.
:refuse reasoning /Unstratifiable negation: strongly-connected component containing/
all $x: person($x) & ~secure($x) -> prisoner($x).
:refuse reasoning /Unstratifiable negation: strongly-connected component containing/
all $x: person($x) & ~suffice($x) -> prisoner($x).
